    text: "<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; margin-top: 12px;\">\n      <svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 18 18\" style=\"flex: none; vertical-align: middle;\"><path d=\"M9 2 L16.5 15 H1.5 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c5e86c\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M9 7 V10.5\" stroke=\"#c5e86c\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"12.7\" r=\"1\" fill=\"#c5e86c\"/></svg>\n      <span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; color: #c5e86c;\">Backfire</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #e8e8ee; margin-top: 6px;\">\n      Sometimes a skill goes wrong and does the opposite, for its whole <span class=\"term\">chain</span>: an attack hits your own squad, a heal heals the enemy, a Guard steps aside and the slam lands on your weakest ally. Tired units backfire more often: 3% when fresh, up to 30% when worn out.\n    </div>",
